        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$x$ and $y$ as functions of $t$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=20t$, $y=-5t^2+15t+50$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}\\cos\\theta&=\\frac45,\\qquad \\sin\\theta=\\frac35\\\\ \\dot{x}&=25\\left(\\frac45\\right)=20\\\\ \\dot{y}(0)&=25\\left(\\frac35\\right)=15\\\\ x&=20t\\qquad (x(0)=0)\\\\ y&=-5t^2+15t+C\\\\ y(0)&=50\\quad\\text{so }C=50\\\\ y&=-5t^2+15t+50\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 33
      },
      {
        "id": "p27-q6-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "The time to land.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$5\\text{ s}$.",
          "worked": "At ground level, $y=0$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}5t^2-15t-50&=0\\\\ t^2-3t-10&=0\\\\ (t-5)(t+2)&=0\\\\ t&=5\\text{ s}\\end{aligned}$$\nDiscard $t=-2$ because time after launch is positive.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
